    },
    "body": "Currently, popt fails to concatenate long lines split using the terminating \\ character.\n\nA failing example is `/usr/lib/rpm/rpmpopt-X.Y.Z` from RPM that contains a lot of alias definitions. Joining all split lines in a single line, or converting all CRLF to LF in that file, fixes alias machinery.\n\nWe could convert `rpmpopt-X.Y.Z` to LF when building, but that's a fragile solution and will not help with other popt files. We need to add proper CRLF handling to popt itself, just as we added .exe handling a while ago.\n\nShould be easy to fix.",
    "reactions": {
